  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question-42
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 'Why was there no colour change on the part which

    was inside
    the tube having KOH?'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The KOH solution present inside the tube absorbed all the carbon
    dioxide molecules due to which photosynthesis did not occur, resulting in the
    absence of starch from that part of the leaf. As there was no starch present,
    the leaf which was inside the tube did not change its colour.
  options:
  - Due to the absence of starch
  - Photosynthesis did not occur
  - Both (A) and (B)
  - None of these
  correctOptionIndex: 2
